00:24:04.650 --> 00:24:09.370
Live Brady Bunch, which was a bunch of sketch comedy actors.

508
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:16.450
Andy Richter was in the bunch and Jane Lynch, and they did this in LA in the early 90s.

509
00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:16.990
I saw it in LA.

510
00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:17.750
Okay.

511
00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:19.050
I saw it in LA.

512
00:24:19.230 --> 00:24:23.730
It was like a live, satirical, comedic Brady Bunch.

513
00:24:24.270 --> 00:24:24.750
Exactly.

514
00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:30.370
They would do an episode every week and they'd have like a game show element beforehand and

515
00:24:30.370 --> 00:24:34.770
they made it really groovy in 70s and it just became like a cool thing to go see.

516
00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:40.810
And they were replacing the Marsha for like a month because she had gotten a pilot or something.

517
00:24:40.810 --> 00:24:46.870
So my roommate at the time read about it in one of those, you know, breakdowns.

518
00:24:46.870 --> 00:24:47.950
Like backstage WeSt.

519
00:24:48.090 --> 00:24:48.990
Yes, exactly.

520
00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:49.250
Yeah.

521
00:24:49.290 --> 00:24:49.610
Exactly.

522
00:24:49.770 --> 00:24:53.270
And she just said, you know, you should go in on this.

523
00:24:53.490 --> 00:24:57.350
Like you should get an audition for this because you're so Brady obsessed.

524
00:24:57.630 --> 00:24:59.490
Like it was no surprise.

525
00:24:59.490 --> 00:25:03.330
Like everyone in my life knew that I loved the Brady Bunch.

526
00:25:03.450 --> 00:25:09.210
So I asked my agents about it and I went in and auditioned and I really feel like it

527
00:25:09.210 --> 00:25:11.050
