00:27:07.470 --> 00:27:10.270
And I don't feel that way about most auditions.

569
00:27:10.470 --> 00:27:15.030
Most auditions, I think, well, listen, I could do a great job, but probably so could someone

570
00:27:15.030 --> 00:27:15.430
else.

571
00:27:15.790 --> 00:27:15.930
Right.

572
00:27:15.930 --> 00:27:22.670
But for Pam, I felt like deep in my bones and ownership of this character, I felt like

573
00:27:22.670 --> 00:27:24.430
this is why I became an actor.

574
00:27:25.090 --> 00:27:30.550
I'll do many other things, I'm sure, but this is why I got in this business in the first

575
00:27:30.550 --> 00:27:30.790
place.

576
00:27:30.910 --> 00:27:36.030
And so I'm just curious, where were you internally as you're auditioning for this role?

577
00:27:36.030 --> 00:27:45.670
Well, you nailed it, but I knew it in my core that there was nobody who could do it better

578
00:27:45.670 --> 00:27:46.130
than me.

579
00:27:46.470 --> 00:27:46.890
Yeah.

580
00:27:47.070 --> 00:27:52.150
And whether or not they saw that, you know, and this was, by the way, it wasn't like I

